1
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:14,140
Dad.

2
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:24,600
Dad.

3
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:38,040
I want you to break the contract right now

4
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:41,000
and give my dad back his chance to reincarnate.

5
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:47,600
I can't do that.

6
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:49,300
Why?

7
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:51,400
Why can't you?

8
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:54,800
It's not that I don't want to,

9
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:57,560
but I have no way to wake him up either.

10
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:01,740
Then let's start over again.

11
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,860
Let everything go back to the beginning.

12
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:05,600
I'll pretend I never met you.

13
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:08,930
Even if time turns back,

14
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:10,780
an injured soul

15
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:12,690
cannot be restored.

16
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:26,000
You are a murderer.

17
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:28,900
You've been one for a thousand years.

18
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:31,730
You'll do anything to achieve your goals.

19
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:34,660
At first, I didn't know your identities in your past lives.

20
00:01:34,660 --> 00:01:35,840
In your eyes,

21
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:37,640
can the soul of an insignificant person

22
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,340
be taken away by you at will?

23
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:40,960
No, listen to me.

24
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:41,539
Enough.

25
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:44,360
Selfishness is your nature.

26
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:47,800
It's been deeply rooted in your soul for a long time.

27
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,870
The reason you act like this

28
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:53,670
is nothing more than to make up for your hypocritical guilt.

29
00:01:55,460 --> 00:01:57,060
It's really terrifying.

30
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,520
What exactly did my dad and I do wrong

31
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:04,160
to have to meet you in every lifetime?

32
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,240
I'm begging you.

33
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:08,919
Let me go.

34
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:10,880
Let my dad go.

35
00:02:11,660 --> 00:02:12,420
Can you?

36
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:15,300
Stop acting like an evil spirit

37
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:17,340
and pestering us, okay?

38
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:09,200
What brings you here?

39
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:34,080
You rascal.

40
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:36,880
This is nonsense.

41
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,260
Is there any other way?

42
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:44,920
A way?

43
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:46,640
There is one.

44
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:49,780
But the price is a bit high.

45
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:50,600
What is it?

46
00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:53,270
You must inject your soul power

47
00:05:53,540 --> 00:05:54,800
into the other person.

48
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:58,080
Until your soul dissipates

49
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:01,560
and turns to dust.

50
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:10,800
If it were you,

51
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:12,580
what would you do?

52
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:14,980
That depends

53
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:18,340
on what you are doing this for.

54
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:26,680
Please annul our engagement

55
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:28,400
and set me free.

56
00:06:39,180 --> 00:06:40,580
It's because of that man.

57
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:44,480
Do you really think he is sincere to you?

58
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:46,940
Don't be silly.

59
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:49,180
Do you know who he is?

60
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:51,460
He is the First Prince.

61
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:59,300
He is the culprit who caused your father's death.

62
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:03,440
Impossible.

63
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:14,480
When the two armies were at war,

64
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:18,500
the First Prince deserted out of fear of the slaughter,

65
00:07:18,780 --> 00:07:20,910
causing the frontline to lose morale.

66
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:23,540
In the end, it was your father

67
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:26,160
who took the blame for him.

68
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:30,140
You actually had the delusion

69
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:32,470
of eloping with him.

70
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:35,680
How ridiculous.

71
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:41,600
Think about it.

72
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:46,170
Haven't you always wanted to avenge your father and clear his name?

73
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:51,060
Now you have the chance.

74
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:53,480
Kill him.

75
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:56,240
Then you can avenge your father.

76
00:07:56,980 --> 00:08:00,380
I will immediately break off our engagement and set you free.

77
00:08:08,140 --> 00:08:09,670
Think it through yourself.

78
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:27,400
An abandoned prince.

79
00:08:28,940 --> 00:08:29,760
Why kill him?

80
00:08:30,340 --> 00:08:31,140
No.

81
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:33,179
Only if he dies

82
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:36,820
can the Second Prince be at ease.

83
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:49,920
Why?

84
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,360
Murderer.

85
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:45,840
Tang'er.

86
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:57,240
Mafeisan.

87
00:10:01,660 --> 00:10:04,680
This blade severs all grudges and affections.

88
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:07,900
From now on, we are strangers.

89
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:21,440
Miss Tang'er.

90
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:23,720
How did it go?

91
00:10:33,740 --> 00:10:34,680
From now on,

92
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:37,600
I have nothing to do with Prince Ling's Mansion.

93
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:39,060
We owe each other nothing.

94
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:44,160
This female thief assassinated the prince.

95
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:45,490
Kill her without mercy.

96
00:10:52,780 --> 00:10:53,880
I expected this.

97
00:10:57,340 --> 00:10:58,140
Stop.

98
00:10:58,840 --> 00:10:59,640
Stop.

99
00:11:20,980 --> 00:11:21,800
Tang'er.

100
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:26,860
Tang'er.

101
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,480
Chenyao.

102
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:55,000
Kill him.

103
00:12:08,940 --> 00:12:09,800
Your Highness.

104
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:11,600
Let me explain.

105
00:12:11,640 --> 00:12:12,280
It... It's her.

106
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:13,380
She killed you.

107
00:12:13,380 --> 00:12:15,640
I was helping you get rid of this traitor.

108
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:17,140
I deserve to die.

109
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:18,070
I deserve to die.

110
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:19,880
It's the Second Prince.

111
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:21,210
It's the Second Prince.

112
00:12:36,700 --> 00:12:37,520
Tang'er.

113
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:47,520
Tang'er.

114
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:50,260
Tang'er.

115
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:03,500
It's all because of me

116
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:05,730
that you and your father suffered.

117
00:13:31,140 --> 00:13:31,840
Maybe...

118
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:34,880
I'm just trying to atone for my sins.

119
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:37,280
Who asked you to atone?

120
00:13:38,180 --> 00:13:40,120
It's been lifetimes.

121
00:13:40,140 --> 00:13:42,270
Why are you still clinging to the past?

122
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:45,720
You need to learn to let go,

123
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:47,820
look forward to things,

124
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:50,540
feel the present with your heart,

125
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:54,100
and bravely embrace the beauty of the future.

126
00:13:56,220 --> 00:13:57,580
Can I really let go?

127
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:59,100
Of course.

128
00:13:59,820 --> 00:14:00,680
Think about it.

129
00:14:01,020 --> 00:14:03,340
You're only a few years away from a thousand years of service.

130
00:14:03,340 --> 00:14:04,280
Is it worth it?

131
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:06,920
Given our relationship,

132
00:14:06,940 --> 00:14:08,480
I'll ask the higher-ups

133
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:10,160
and get you

134
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:12,300
a more relaxing position, okay?

135
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:25,110
I've figured it out.

136
00:14:25,140 --> 00:14:27,180
Exactly. Isn't that better?

137
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:28,800
Go on.

138
00:14:30,180 --> 00:14:32,780
Remember, don't come empty-handed next time.

139
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:46,080
This kid.

140
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:55,280
Wait a minute.

141
00:14:56,380 --> 00:14:58,720
If he's still clinging to the past,

142
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:02,720
why did he grab that key?

143
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:20,880
Mr. Gu.

144
00:15:22,740 --> 00:15:24,740
I just got news from the private investigator.

145
00:15:24,740 --> 00:15:25,920
They said they found Mu Chen and Hao Zhenshi.

146
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:26,620
Where are they?

147
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:29,120
The message says they're in an abandoned building.

148
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:29,920
Let's go then.

149
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:30,980
We don't have time.

150
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:32,510
The trial is about to start.

151
00:15:35,580 --> 00:15:36,580
Call the police.

152
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:38,380
We can't call the police.

153
00:15:39,180 --> 00:15:41,180
I thought about calling the police too.

154
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:43,320
But I'm afraid the police will provoke him.

155
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:45,340
He might resort to extreme measures

156
00:15:45,340 --> 00:15:47,140
and take everyone down with him.

157
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:50,220
Then what do you suggest?

158
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:52,920
There's only one way now.

159
00:15:54,020 --> 00:15:54,880
Let Chen Yao go.

160
00:15:56,380 --> 00:15:57,200
Him?

161
00:15:58,380 --> 00:15:59,280
He can't go.

162
00:15:59,740 --> 00:16:00,540
What?

163
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:03,020
Where did he go?

164
00:16:03,620 --> 00:16:04,620
I... I don't know.

165
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:08,410
Did something happen between you two?

166
00:16:12,420 --> 00:16:13,160
Lawyer Gu.

167
00:16:13,660 --> 00:16:15,740
At a critical moment like this,

168
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:18,410
are we going to fail at the last minute?

169
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:20,720
Hurry up and find him to bring him back.

170
00:16:20,720 --> 00:16:21,920
Where am I supposed to find him?

171
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:23,520
What are you hesitating for?

172
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:25,420
You know how cunning Ling Hengsheng is.

173
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:26,750
This is our only chance.

174
00:16:27,780 --> 00:16:28,320
I got it.

175
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,420
What do you know?

176
00:16:30,580 --> 00:16:31,840
Then tell me who should go.

177
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:32,780
The police?

178
00:16:32,780 --> 00:16:33,620
Or you?

179
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:34,820
I'll go.

180
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:40,380
Brother Chen.

181
00:16:40,940 --> 00:16:42,280
I'm glad you're here.

182
00:16:42,820 --> 00:16:44,150
Don't yell at her again.

183
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:47,080
Yes.

184
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:49,140
I was just too anxious.

185
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:54,150
I found a way to wake your father up.

186
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:56,100
When all this is over,

187
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:57,940
I will definitely wake him up.

188
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:03,980
Give me the address.

189
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:05,780
You guys head to the court first.

190
00:17:05,819 --> 00:17:06,619
Okay.
